      "question": "C has parametric equations x = 1/t + 2, y = (1 - 2t)/(3 + t), t > 0. Show that the equation of C can be written as y = g(x) = (ax + b)/(cx + d), x > k, where a, b, c, d and k are integers to be found.",
      "status": "ready",
      "answer": "a = 1, b = -4, c = 3, d = -5, k = 2, so g(x) = (x - 4)/(3x - 5), x > 2",
      "steps": [
        "From x = 1/t + 2 get 1/t = x - 2, so t = 1/(x - 2).",
        "Substitute into y: the numerator 1 - 2t becomes (x - 4)/(x - 2).",
        "The denominator 3 + t becomes (3x - 5)/(x - 2).",
        "Divide the two: y = (x - 4)/(3x - 5).",
        "Since t > 0, x = 1/t + 2 > 2, so k = 2."
      ],
