      "question": "A curve C has parametric equations x = t/(t - 3), y = 1/t + 2, t in R, t > 3. Show that all points on C lie on the curve with Cartesian equation y = (ax - 1)/(bx), where a and b are constants to be found.",
      "status": "ready",
      "answer": "y = (7x - 1)/(3x), so a = 7 and b = 3",
      "steps": [
