        "Write x = t/(t - 3) = 1/(1 - 3/t).",
        "Substitute 1/t: x = 1/(1 - 3(y - 2)) = 1/(7 - 3y).",
        "Rearrange: 7x - 3xy = 1, so 3xy = 7x - 1.",
        "Hence y = (7x - 1)/(3x), giving a = 7 and b = 3."
