      "question": "The curve C has parametric equations x = 3 + 2 sin t, y = 6/(7 + cos 2t), -pi/2 <= t <= pi/2. Show that C has Cartesian equation y = 12/((7 - x)(1 + x)), p <= x <= q, where p and q are constants to be found.",
